silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_yoneda_hom_leg_3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderLegValidateExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_yoneda_hom_leg_3 silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeUngatedRenderLegValidate', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §13.5 plus the SHACL shape-conformance discipline of paper 24: the validate arrow fires a typed-shape check on TypedClaim. For the Mittens MeasurementEvent2024 fixture, the SHACL MeasurementEventShape requires mass-positive, date-ISO8601-parseable, quality-is-BodyMassQuality. ValidatedClaim is produced iff the shape passes; otherwise the chain halts with a SHACL refusal. The probe holds because render cannot fire without ValidatedClaim as its source." .
